$(
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=
  Foulis-Holland theorem
=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=-=
$)

  $( Foulis-Holland Theorem.  If any 2 pairs in a triple of orthomodular
     lattice elements commute, the triple is distributive.  First of two parts.
     Theorem 5 of [Kalmbach] p. 25.  (Contributed by NM, 14-Jun-2006.)
     (New usage is discouraged.) $)
  fh1 $p |- ( ( ( A e. CH /\ B e. CH /\ C e. CH ) /\ ( A C_H B /\ A C_H C ) )
             -> ( A i^i ( B vH C ) ) = ( ( A i^i B ) vH ( A i^i C ) ) ) $=
    ( cch wcel ccm wbr wa cin chj cort cfv c0h wceq chincl sylan2 adantr ineq2d
    co eqtrd w3a csh wss chjcl syl2an anandis chsh syl jca 3impb ledi incom a1i
    chdmj1 chdmm1 ineqan12d ineq12d 3impdi inass cmcm2 wb choccl cmbr3 3adantl3
    bitrd biimpa adantrr 3adantl2 adantrl inindi eqtrid in12 eqtrdi chocin chm0
    3eqtr4g eqtr3d sylan9eqr pjoml syl12anc eqcomd ) ADEZBDEZCDEZUAZABFGZACFGZH
    ZHZABIZACIZJSZABCJSZIZWIWLDEZWNUBEZHZWLWNUCZWNWLKLZIZMNWLWNNWEWQWHWBWCWDWQW
    BWCWDHZHZWOWPWBWCWDWOWBWCHZWJDEZWKDEZWOWBWDHZABOZACOZWJWKUDUEUFXBWNDEZWPXAW
    BWMDEZXIBCUDZAWMOPWNUGUHUIUJQWEWRWHABCUKQWIWTWMAIZAKLZBKLZJSZXMCKLZJSZIZIZM
    WEWTXSNZWHWBWCWDXTXCXFHZWNXLWSXRWNXLNYAAWMULUMYAWSWJKLZWKKLZIZXRXCXDXEWSYDN
