  ${
    $d x A $.  $d x B $.
    $( The Hilbert lattice has the covering property.  Proposition 1(ii) of
       [Kalmbach] p. 140 (and its converse).  (Contributed by NM, 11-Jun-2004.)
       (New usage is discouraged.) $)
    chcv1 $p |- ( ( A e. CH /\ B e. HAtoms ) ->
                ( -. B C_ A <-> A <oH ( A vH B ) ) ) $=
      ( vx cch wcel cat wa wss wn chj co ccv wbr cv c0v wne csn cspn chba wi
      wceq wrex atom1d spansncv2 sseq1 notbid breq2d imbi12d syl5ibrcom adantld
      cfv oveq2 rexlimdva sylan2b atelch wpss chjcl cvpss syldan sylibrd sylan2
      imp chnle impbid ) ADEZBFEZGBAHZIZAABJKZLMZVFVECNZOPZBVKQRUKZUAZGZCSUBZVH
